42-
43-- describe the sheet as one flat magenta **field**, never as a "grid of cells" — the word *grid* made the model draw an actual grid, with white panels and magenta rules (take 3);
44-- draw references from exactly **ONE** existing camera angle — mixed angles make it produce a turnaround instead of a walk cycle (takes 4–5, and the first take of `jumper-n`, `jumper-w` and all eight diagonals);
45-- name the asymmetric prop **explicitly**: the Baron's hat card rides his body-RIGHT and must be INVISIBLE from an east camera. Takes 4–5 put it on, which is the mirror signature the sheet law forbids — and main's own east row agrees with me, it has no card;
46-- spell the four/eight walk phases out as distinct moments (contact / down / passing / up) — the generic wording gave four near-identical poses (`school-e` take 1).
